From f4a15ed848a2b8c3ee7d26b1640c51f048393ff7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Lassoff <jof@thejof.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:20:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Boot splash: BIOS draws a spinner and progress bar until
 a host takes over

From power-on the BIOS clears framebuffer bank 2, draws a spinner and a
five-step bar there, shows it, and animates it every 80 ms. It stops
drawing once base_addr points at another bank, and resumes if pointed
back. The bar shows ctrl_scratch (1-5), so a host can report its boot
progress with one CSR write.

The CPU writes the SDRAM through a new CsrDramWriter, a whole 64-bit
word at a time: the board grounds the SDRAM's DQM pins, so narrower
writes would clobber the rest of the word. Its three CSRs go at the end
of the hub75_soc bank, so no existing CSR address moves.
