--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -44,6 +44,22 @@ The Hub75Controller reads frames from DRAM into row buffers. Hub75Drivers
 send the row buffers to the panels. Then the Hub75Controller drives the latch,
 row address, and output enable signals.
 
+## Boot splash
+
+Until a host sends frames, the BIOS (`bios/splash.c`) draws a spinner and a
+five-step progress bar into framebuffer bank 2 (32-bit word 98304 on) and
+displays it. It leaves bank 2 alone once `base_addr` points elsewhere, and
+resumes if it's pointed back. The bar shows `ctrl_scratch` (1-5; the BIOS sets
+1), so a host can report its own boot progress with one CSR write.
+
+The CPU writes the SDRAM through `CsrDramWriter`: `fb_address` sets a 64-bit
+word address, and each write to `fb_data_hi` commits `{fb_data_hi, fb_data_lo}`
+and steps on. The board grounds the SDRAM's DQM pins, so only whole 64-bit
+words can be written safely.
+
+The splash's panel layout (a 2x2 of 64x64 panels on slots 9, 15, 7 and 1) is
+compiled in.
+
 # Installation
 
